            <ArticleTitle>Gastrointestinal blood loss on phenylbutazone and feprazone.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>108-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Feprazone, a new anti-inflammatory drug, is a useful antirheumatic preparation which causes little gastrointestinal upset. This short cross-over study shows no significant gastrointestinal blood loss with either feprazone or phenylbutazone by the red-cell chromium-51 labelling method.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
